<</Type/Annot/Subtype/FreeText/P 18 0 R/F 4/M(D:20251118194645+06'00')/NM(b598805f-09fd-48ea-bd01-33fcae61e174)/Contents(Since each data point is independent, during likelihood calculation, we multiply the probability of each data point. Because each value is less than 1, multiplying many probabilities makes the overall value very small, approaching zero, which is difficult for comparison. That's why we take the logarithm of each probability and add these log values instead of multiplying, making comparisons easier. This is called log-likelihood. When calculating the error, it doesn't have negative values; this is known as NLL. The smaller its value, the better.)/CA 1/CreationDate(D:20251118194046+06'00')/IT/FreeTextTypewriter/BS<</Type/Border/W 0/S/S>>/Rotate 0/DA(11.760000 TL /Helv 10.500000 Tf 0 .466667 .831373 rg 0 .466667 .831373 RG )/AP<</N 2533 0 R>>/Rect[ 60.558011 402.722596 954 438.112098]/C[ 0 .466667 .831373]>>
